  "name": "Joropo central (Tuy valleys harp joropo)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Joropo central, or joropo tuyero, is the harp joropo of the Tuy valleys of Miranda and of Aragua in north-central Venezuela, distinct from the plains joropo llanero. Its arpa central (arpa tuyera or mirandina) has metal strings in the treble, and the usual group is only harp and maracas, the maraquero often being the singer, in pasajes and in the revuelta, a linked suite of sections. The arpa llanera card stands in for the arpa central.",
